<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY TWELVE-MONTH BILL YIELD RISES TO 19.72 PCT.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY TWELVE-MONTH BILL YIELD RISES TO 19.72 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of twelve-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 19.72 percent, up from 19.64 percent at an auction two weeks ago, the Government Debt Management Agency said.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	    17,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     37,813.15 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	   17,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		22,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    19.72 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     83.5659 pct</p>
</text>
